preConditionHook:
// EL: AbsValue(close - close[lookback]) < netAtr * WFSafe_AvgTrueRange(atrLength)
// -- no directional progress over the window (G04-10), the second half of
// Grimes's random-walk trading-range read (merge decision 8). The containment
// half is RangeWidthBelowAtrMultiple at its own defaults; the two AND in one
// pane.
//
// NOT Momentum negated: that rule is one-sided and mirrored, so its negation is
// still one bound on one side. This is a two-sided band on the same lagged
// difference with IDENTICAL text on both sides.
//
// WFSafe_AvgTrueRange is MultiWalk's ROLLING accumulator, not a fresh mean:
// seeded with a full N-term sum on the study's first calculated bar, thereafter
// S += TrueRange; S -= TrueRange[Length]; as TWO statements (EasyLanguage
// evaluates S[1] + in - out left to right and folding it rounds differently),
// and re-seeded when the length changes. AtrProfitTarget is the reference.
//
// Deepest bar touched: max(lookback, atrLength + 1).
if (atrLen != (int)atrLength) {
    atrSum = 0.0;
    for (int i = 0; i < (int)atrLength; ++i) {
        double hi = high[i] > close[i + 1] ? high[i] : close[i + 1];
        double lo = low[i] < close[i + 1] ? low[i] : close[i + 1];
        atrSum += hi - lo;
    }
    atrLen = (int)atrLength;
} else {
    const int out = (int)atrLength;
    double hiIn = high[0] > close[1] ? high[0] : close[1];
    double loIn = low[0] < close[1] ? low[0] : close[1];
    double hiOut = high[out] > close[out + 1] ? high[out] : close[out + 1];
    double loOut = low[out] < close[out + 1] ? low[out] : close[out + 1];
    atrSum += hiIn - loIn;
    atrSum -= hiOut - loOut;
}
atr = atrSum / (int)atrLength;
